WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.515 --> 00:00:01.890
 The only rule
for eating a taco

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:04.620
is that once you have it
ready, you don't put it down.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:05.655
You just finish it.

00:00:05.655 --> 00:00:06.525
[LAUGHS]

00:00:06.525 --> 00:00:07.395
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.395 --> 00:00:10.650
I grew up in a
family where food was the glue

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:14.250
of everything, cooking, eating,
and sitting around a table

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:17.910
brings people together in
a way that few things do.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.710
I never set out
to become a chef.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:23.010
I opened a restaurant, and it
was a farm-to-table restaurant

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:25.820
in Mexico City when that
was not the general trend.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.310
It was so successful that
I turned it into my career.

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:31.830
This class is for
everybody and anybody

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.190
who's interested in food.

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:36.600
It's important to know about
other cultures through food.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.690
I'm going to teach you how to
make a few delicious salsas.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:42.070
Oh, my goodness, it's so good.

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:46.020
Pescado ala talla, tuna
tostadas, aguachile,

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:50.580
tamales, and I'm going to teach
you how to make tortillas.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.640
From age 7, I became the
resident tortilla maker

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:54.610
in my house.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:56.710
It was the first thing
I learned to cook.

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:58.658
It's actually a
fairly easy process.

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.450
There's nothing like
a fresh-made tortilla.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:01.930
There really isn't.

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:05.280
We're going to make tacos al
pastor, the dish of Mexico

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:05.790
City.

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:07.010
And it's a street food.

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:11.200
It's a rub with chiles,
fresh vegetables, and spices.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.195
The aroma is really enticing.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:18.800
That is so good.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.810
It's very typical
of Mexican culture

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:22.328
to start the day off with eggs.

00:01:22.328 --> 00:01:24.370
We're going to make huevos
rancheros divorciados,

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:26.580
using a green sauce
and a red sauce.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:28.773
I'm going to put a
little bit of water.

00:01:28.773 --> 00:01:30.440
They're going to roast
for half an hour.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:34.400
And meanwhile, we do nothing.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.800
[LAUGHS]

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:39.380
I really urge you
to pay attention

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:42.680
to every bit of what you
put into the dish, just

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:47.030
in a way in which you
translate your enjoyment.

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:49.445
Está delicioso.

00:01:49.445 --> 00:01:52.730
And I know it's not always
easy, but the more one

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:55.160
can connect with
people over a shared

00:01:55.160 --> 00:02:00.440
love of a delightful dish, the
better off your result will be.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:05.230
I am Gabriela Cámara, and
this is my MasterClass.

